/**
@defgroup grp_app Application core
@brief Menu logic and device state: decides which screen is shown and what the button does.

**Responsibility**
- Owns the device state machine: startup, menu, Live Data, Device info.
- Turns button events into navigation. Short press moves to the next entry, long press selects.
- Hands data to the UI and to the USB module. It does not touch hardware directly.

**Depends on:** @ref grp_input, @ref grp_sensor, @ref grp_display, @ref grp_usb, @ref grp_logging.

**Epics:** \jira{KAN-5}, \jira{KAN-8}
*/

/**
@defgroup grp_display Display UI (TouchGFX)
@brief Screens, drawing and the LCD: startup image, menu, Live Data screen, Device info screen.

**Responsibility**
- Draw the 240x320 screens designed in Figma (repo `pulsar-ui-ux`).
- Live Data screen: numeric values plus a scrolling graph of the gyroscope axes.
- Keep the frame buffer in the external SDRAM. One RGB565 frame is 240 x 320 x 2 B = 153,600 B.

**Constraints**
- TouchGFX is generated by Designer into `pulsar-touchgfx`. Hand-written code stays in `gui/`.
- TouchGFX with CMake is not proven yet. @jira{KAN-12} answers this.

**Epics:** \jira{KAN-5}, \jira{KAN-6}, \jira{KAN-12}
*/

/**
@defgroup grp_sensor Sensor service
@brief Samples the on-board gyroscope and provides the values to the application and the USB module.

**Responsibility**
- Read the gyroscope over SPI5 at a fixed rate and convert the raw values to physical units.
- Provide the latest sample and a stream of samples.

**Open design points:** sample rate, filtering, units, buffer size (to be fixed in the LLD).

**Epics:** \jira{KAN-4}
*/

/**
@defgroup grp_input Button input
@brief Reads the user button B1 (PA0) and produces short-press and long-press events.

**Responsibility**
- Debounce the button.
- Short press: next. Long press: select. The long-press time is proposed as about 0.8 s.

**Epics:** \jira{KAN-5}
*/

/**
@defgroup grp_usb USB CDC and protocol
@brief USB device (CDC) link to the PC tool: sensor stream out, commands in.

**Responsibility**
- Present the board as a virtual serial port (CDC) to the PC.
- Frame the data stream and the commands. The protocol is still open (text or binary).
- Keep the data stream separate from the log output.

**Note:** CubeMX currently configures USB as Host. It must change to Device CDC (@jira{KAN-3}).

**Epics:** \jira{KAN-3}, \jira{KAN-4}, \jira{KAN-7}
*/

/**
@defgroup grp_logging Logging
@brief Leveled, tagged log messages from all modules, safe to call from tasks and interrupts.

**Responsibility**
- Levels, module tags, timestamps, low overhead, compile-time disable.
- Ring buffer and a low-priority log task. First sink: UART or ITM. USB later.

**Epics:** \jira{KAN-13}
*/

/**
@defgroup grp_platform Platform (CubeMX, FreeRTOS)
@brief Generated hardware layer: HAL, clock, FreeRTOS, startup. Owned by CubeMX.

**Responsibility**
- Clock at 180 MHz (currently 72 MHz), GPIO, SPI5, LTDC, FMC SDRAM, USB.
- FreeRTOS (CMSIS-RTOS v1). The application runs from the default task through `app_loop()`.
- Changed only through CubeMX, hooks only inside USER CODE blocks.

**Epics:** \jira{KAN-3}
*/
